<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Acanthometra pellucida Schnakenberg wavelength at 206 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma), pass 2 — MorphoEval overall 85.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes the three pass-1 remediations. Held-out wavelength RMSE is 6.09 nm against an in-sample RMSE of 43.30 nm; Pearson r stays 0.9991. Both ablations collapse the field. The carrier is visible on the capsule and cv_sim_similarity is 92.8 (12 frames, 680 px). Radial-profile r fell from 0.548 to 0.096 because the disk is now the spot field rather than a flat fill under crossing spines. Weighted score 85.6. Open items remain a species-level photo, the radial-profile miss, n = 3 on the held-out split, and a second assessor. Overall 85.6/100 (faithfulness 84.6, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit f1fee7075fcbec51969593b452b4632c61bd2928; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py at f1fee7075fcbec51969593b452b4632c61bd2928, image/png, 688006 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 f35dc4b0b74fce257c0fa2cc609f91bf704de3e79d1d0e29c093724b48f66fd4 (sha256 f35dc4b0b74fce257c0fa2cc609f91bf704de3e79d1d0e29c093724b48f66fd4), spec_fingerprint e39627dd2e1ab0061d44983f5e20e147e309799aaead4a87c95c97412dce57d6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: e39627dd2e1ab0061d44983f5e20e147e309799aaead4a87c95c97412dce57d6; artifact_sha256: f35dc4b0b74fce257c0fa2cc609f91bf704de3e79d1d0e29c093724b48f66fd4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0/acanthometra_pellucida_specimen.jpg=f07186d3f18203f0..., datasets/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=879c1b1d04423021...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952), Gierer and Meinhardt (1972), and Murray (1981) supply the reaction-diffusion wavelength law. | Haeckel (1904) Tafel 21 figure 2 is the vendored drawing. Decelle et al. (2012) is living-acantharian biology, not a 206 nm measurement.; reconstructed_in_script: In-sample Pearson r = 0.9991 (RMSE 43.30 nm) and a held-out scale of 1.1875 fit on gamma 4, 7, 10 and scored on 14, 19, 26 (r = 0.9991, p = 0.027, n = 3, RMSE 6.09 nm). | Equal-diffusion ratio 0.0004 and autocatalysis-knockout ratio about 0. Spine axes and foreground, coherency, and circularity are measured on the plate and on the last frame, and they are not equal.; transfer_boundary: 206 nm and 0 Ma are the assigned detail scale and the Holocene terminal of a one-point chronoseries. The plate does not resolve 206 nm.; does_not_claim: That the held-out test, with n = 3 and p = 0.027, is a high-powered confirmation. | That the radial gray profile of the carrier matches the plate (r = 0.096). | A species-level photograph of A. pellucida, or a fossil chronospecies.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Open. A photograph identified as Acanthometra pellucida, rather than Haeckel's genus plate.",
        "remediation needed: Open. Held-out n = 3 gives p = 0.027. A finer gamma grid would make that split informative.",
        "remediation needed: Open. Radial gray-profile r is 0.096. The carrier does not reproduce the plate's central star, and it should not be forced to by copying the profile.",
        "remediation needed: Open. Second assessor from another provider. Lean was not executed (no lean binary)." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.56e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Acanthometra pellucida Schnakenberg wavelength at 206 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma), pass 2 — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Wavelength falls as gamma rises, for both the formula and the FFT peak. d = 1 and the autocatalysis knockout each drive std(u) to about 0 while d = 18 reaches std 0.17. The held-out scale is one number, fit on three gammas and applied to three others, and it moves RMSE from 43.30 nm to 6.09 nm." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

