    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Acanthometra pellucida Schnakenberg wavelength at 206 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma), pass 2 (Acanthometra pellucida)",
        "Acanthometra pellucida Schnakenberg wavelength at 206 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma), pass 2 faithfully reproduces Acanthometra pellucida morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Acanthometra pellucida specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Acanthometra pellucida" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A species-level photograph of A. pellucida, or a fossil chronospecies.",
        "does_not_claim: That the held-out test, with n = 3 and p = 0.027, is a high-powered confirmation.",
        "does_not_claim: That the radial gray profile of the carrier matches the plate (r = 0.096).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Equal-diffusion ratio 0.0004 and autocatalysis-knockout ratio about 0. Spine axes and foreground, coherency, and circularity are measured on the plate and on the last frame, and they are not equal.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: In-sample Pearson r = 0.9991 (RMSE 43.30 nm) and a held-out scale of 1.1875 fit on gamma 4, 7, 10 and scored on 14, 19, 26 (r = 0.9991, p = 0.027, n = 3, RMSE 6.09 nm).",
        "reported_in_source: Haeckel (1904) Tafel 21 figure 2 is the vendored drawing. Decelle et al. (2012) is living-acantharian biology, not a 206 nm measurement.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952), Gierer and Meinhardt (1972), and Murray (1981) supply the reaction-diffusion wavelength law.",
        "transfer_boundary: 206 nm and 0 Ma are the assigned detail scale and the Holocene terminal of a one-point chronoseries. The plate does not resolve 206 nm." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Acanthometra pellucida" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mineralized Protists (Silica/Calcite)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Acanthometra" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Acanthometra pellucida; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952), Gierer and Meinhardt (1972), and Murray (1981) supply the reaction-diffusion wavelength law. | Haeckel (1904) Tafel 21 figure 2 is the vendored drawing. Decelle et al. (2012) is living-acantharian biology, not a 206 nm measurement.; reconstructed_in_script: In-sample Pearson r = 0.9991 (RMSE 43.30 nm) and a held-out scale of 1.1875 fit on gamma 4, 7, 10 and scored on 14, 19, 26 (r = 0.9991, p = 0.027, n = 3, RMSE 6.09 nm). | Equal-diffusion ratio 0.0004 and autocatalysis-knockout ratio about 0. Spine axes and foreground, coherency, and circularity are measured on the plate and on the last frame, and they are not equal.; transfer_boundary: 206 nm and 0 Ma are the assigned detail scale and the Holocene terminal of a one-point chronoseries. The plate does not resolve 206 nm.; does_not_claim: That the held-out test, with n = 3 and p = 0.027, is a high-powered confirmation. | That the radial gray profile of the carrier matches the plate (r = 0.096). | A species-level photograph of A. pellucida, or a fossil chronospecies.]; other sources: Kunstformen der Natur, Tafel 21 <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Acanthometra._-_Stachelstrahlinge_LCCN2015648908.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 223 nm (2.232e-07 m, log10=-6.651 m, tier=2_macromolecular_100nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 223 nm to 653 µm): 223 nm:acanthometra-pellucida-bioelectric-polarity, 802 nm:acanthometra-pellucida-vertex-packing, 15 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength, 27 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-clock-wavefront, 46 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-morphogen-condensation, 59 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-flux-canalization, 66 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-elastic-buckling, 76 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-branching-tree" ;
